{
 "answers": {
  "flow": "the spawn sibling 0x15b7a80 produces the error word as word 1 of its stack result; the supervisor reads it from [rsp+8], and on failure (word 0 == 0) stores it back to (rsp) and panics through the thunk 0x1680c30 with (rdx = rsp, rcx = this vtable); the thunk builds two fmt arguments and the adapter 0x1687260 tail-calls the vtable +0x18 method with (value pointer, formatter); on the unwind path the supervisor drops the value by a direct call to the same drop body 0x15be1a0 at 0x15d5c8f",
  "identity": "a Rust one-method trait-object vtable for the 8-byte tagged io error value: drop = its tag-dispatch drop glue 0x15be1a0, size 8, align 8, and the single method is the value's Debug format function (the body at 0x5ca7ea0, reached through the 6-byte PLT stub 0x5ca5610), which renders the std debug-struct forms \"Os\" / \"Error\" / \"Custom\" with \"kind\" and \"message\" fields over the same low-two-bit tag encoding the drop body dispatches on",
  "method": "PLT stub 0x5ca5610 (6 bytes, jmp *0x64e1878) resolving by RELATIVE relocation to body 0x5ca7ea0 (1,237 bytes); convention (rdi = pointer to the 8-byte error value, rsi = &mut Formatter) -> fmt::Result tag in rax (common exit masks al with 1); tag & 3 dispatch through the jump table at 0x948c90 to arms 0x5ca7ecc / 0x5ca80fe / 0x5ca7f3f / 0x5ca8073; the stub is shared by 32 size-8/align-8 vtables in .data.rel.ro, with 30 distinct drops, and by one .got cell (0x64e0170)",
  "references": "exactly one in the whole binary: the lea at 0x15d5c42 in the spawn supervisor 0x15d5b00, into rcx as the fourth argument of its panic call; no other rip-relative use, no movabs, no relocation addend, no raw qword",
  "write_body_relation": "the write body 0x1533d60 of PR #3012 produces values of this exact encoding -- 0 for success (not an error value), (errno << 32) | 2 (tag 2, OS error) and the bare address of the static message datum 0x6400488 (tag 0) -- and drops one by a direct call to 0x15be1a0 on its EINTR path; the method's tag-0 arm dereferences statics of the 0x6400488 layout; the write body never references the vtable itself"
 },
